# Plum-Audio unit table — one line per unit, read by docker/deploy.sh and scripts/host-setup/provision.sh.
#
# COPY THIS FILE to `units.conf` (gitignored) and list your own units. This file lives on your
# WORKSTATION and describes your whole fleet. You write it once, not once per Pi.
#
#   host | name | [audio output]
#
# host           The unit's IP address or hostname. Give every Pi a static address or a DHCP
#                reservation, and put them all on ONE subnet — mDNS is link-local, so units on
#                different VLANs cannot discover each other.
#
# name           What this unit is called. This is the only thing you have to choose.
#                A unit with no settings.json yet adopts it BOTH as its own display name and as the
#                name of every source endpoint it offers, so it is what you see in the mesh view,
#                on the GUI unit cards, and in an AirPlay sender's speaker list.
#                Rename a unit later in Settings and that wins on that unit permanently — this
#                column only decides what an unnamed unit boots as. It is not re-applied by a
#                later deploy.
#                KEEP NAMES UNIQUE. A duplicate does not stop a deploy: deploy.sh appends the Pi's
#                SoC serial (last four hex) and warns, so `Kitchen` twice becomes `Kitchen-EE12`
#                and `Kitchen-A17B`. That is a fallback, not a feature.
#
# audio output   OPTIONAL. Leave it out and deploy.sh reads the unit's sound cards and picks one,
#                preferring a HAT or USB DAC over the onboard jack over HDMI. Fill it in only to
#                override that guess.
#                It is a PortAudio NAME FRAGMENT, matched as a substring against PortAudio's own
#                device names — not an ALSA address. Prefer a card's long name over `hw:C,D`: card
#                NUMBERS move between reboots and the long name does not. `bcm2835` and
#                `snd_rpi_hifiberry_dacplus` are both verified to open at 44100/2/16.
#                Whatever lands here is only what the unit BOOTS with. Settings -> Audio overrides
#                it permanently the first time anyone picks a device, so a wrong guess costs two
#                clicks, not a redeploy.
#
#                `none` is the one value that is not a PortAudio fragment. It means this host has
#                no audio output: deploy.sh selects the headless compose profile (no /dev/snd — the
#                audio profile cannot even be CREATED without it) and expects three supervisord
#                programs instead of four. Such a unit ingests AirPlay/Spotify and routes to other
#                rooms. It renders nothing itself and advertises no speaker.
#
# WHERE THE UNIT IDS WENT
#   This table used to carry a unit id, a player id and a player name as well. Nothing needed an
#   operator to choose them: the container derives the unit id from the Pi's hostname and the
#   player id from the unit id, and deploy.sh keeps whatever id a unit is ALREADY running under, so
#   a redeploy never renames a live unit. Set a unique hostname per Pi in Imager and the ids take
#   care of themselves. A six-column file still works, with a warning.
#
# The addresses below are RFC 5737 documentation addresses and route nowhere.

192.0.2.10  | Kitchen
192.0.2.11  | Living Room
192.0.2.12  | Office      | snd_rpi_hifiberry_dacplus

# A unit with no sound card at all: it ingests AirPlay/Spotify/Bluetooth and routes to other rooms,
# but renders nothing itself.
# 192.0.2.13  | Hallway     | none
